  "slug": "syncora-dashboard-stale-data-check",
  "title": "Checking Whether a Syncora Dashboard Is Showing Older Tally Data",
  "description": "Use timestamps and a specific transaction to decide whether a dashboard reading reflects current TallyPrime data.",
  "category": "Sync troubleshooting",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Compare three points in time",
      "body": "Write down when the source entry was added, when the connector last succeeded and when you opened the dashboard. If the entry is newer than the successful run, you have a clear reason to wait for another sync before judging the result."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Compare a known old and new entry",
      "body": "Open the same company and period in both views. Confirm one older transaction appears and then look for the new one. This helps distinguish a delayed update from a missing company or an overly narrow date filter."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Give your team a clear status",
      "body": "Share an as-of timestamp if someone needs the report before the next successful sync. If the update is still missing after that run, note the company, voucher identity and exact completed time so a colleague can reproduce the check."
    }
  ],
  "relatedPaths": [
    "/guides/tally-sync-troubleshooting",
    "/support"
  ]
}
